:: \ What is Cybersickness? {"position":"700,25","size":"100,100"}
# Cybersickness and sex differences 

Motion sickness during or after VR is common enough to have its own name: ''cybersickness''. Symptoms include nausea, sweating, disorientation, and headache. 

### Have you ever experienced cybersickness?
(link-reveal: "Yes")[
You're not alone. In one study, 65.2% of participants experienced cybersickness after a 10-minute VR session, and 23.9% experienced it severely (Frías-Hiciano et al., 2022).]
(link-reveal: "No")[
Lucky you, but you're in the minority. In one study, 65.2% of participants experienced cybersickness after a 10-minute VR session, and 23.9% experienced it severely (Frías-Hiciano et al., 2022).]

### Sex differences in cybersickness
Studies also suggest women may report it more often, with estimates of the difference ranging from 20 to 40% (Stanney et al., 2020).

[[Why is it higher in women?->Factors]]

(link-reveal: "Click for Sources")[
