:: What is Sexism? {"position":"400,400","size":"100,100"}
# What is Sexism?

Sexism is defined by Swim et al. (2001) as operating as a system of beliefs, language, and behaviors that treat women unfairly based on their gender, expressing itself through everyday stereotyping, patronizing comments, or structural barriers that privilege men over women and gender diverse people.

